Step 1 — Create the GitHub files
Open your Generative-AI-Laboratory repository.

Select Add file → Create new file and create the five files under:

Experiment-08-Real-Time-Speech-Transcription/
Step 2 — Set up Python
Open the experiment folder in VS Code.

Create a virtual environment:

python -m venv .venv



Activate it on Windows PowerShell:

.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1



Step 3 — Install dependencies

python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt



Step 4 — Run the transcription service

python speech_transcription.py



Allow microphone access if your operating system requests permission.
Step 5 — Speak into the microphone
Try saying:
Hello everyone, today we are implementing real-time speech transcription using Python.

Wait for the application to recognize the phrase. It will display the text and save it to the output files.
Step 6 — Stop transcription
Press Ctrl+C in the terminal.

The application will stop listening and display the paths of the generated transcription files.
Step 7 — Verify the results
Open the outputs/ folder.

Check that transcription.txt contains the recognized phrases and transcription_log.csv contains the corresponding timestamps.
